	abstract = {Businesses increasingly recognize the importance of sustainability, profitability, and operational efficiency, particularly in response to global environmental and social challenges. Businesses have a vital role in achieving the sustainable agenda of 2030. The decisions and initiatives of large and small businesses are guided by strategic planning. This study evaluates the alignment of companies' vision statements as declarations of their strategic direction to the United Nations’ Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) statements framed as a multi-criteria decision-making (MCDM) problem using AI-driven semantic similarity analysis. ChatGPT, a large language model (LLM), was used to provide semantic scoring and integrated into the intuitionistic fuzzy to handle the ambiguity in the response of ChatGPT and treated with the Evaluation Based on Distance from Average Solution (EDAS) method to rank the alignment of their strategic direction statement to SDGs. These findings affirm the effectiveness of ChatGPT in semantic alignment evaluation, supporting its reliability in sustainability assessments. The study provides insights into how vision statements reflect the sustainability priorities of the top companies in the Philippines to enhance their strategic alignment with global and national development goals. However, it does not assess overall sustainability performance but focuses on vision statements as guiding frameworks for corporate sustainability initiatives. © 2025 The Authors.},
