	abstract = {As Unmanned Aerial Vehicles (UAVs) power Flying Ad Hoc Networks (FANETs), new paradigms have emerged for next-generation wireless communication, especially in dynamic and mission-critical environments. Embedding 5G capabilities into FANETs enables ultra-reliable, low-latency, and high-throughput communication, but it is also challenging because of energy constraints, high mobility, and frequent topology changes. Based on a hybrid metaheuristic algorithm optimisation (HMAO) strategy, we present an intelligent cluster-based routing framework for 5G-integrated FANETs. A multicriteria approach is used to select cluster heads and maintain clusters, including residual energy, mobility stability, connectivity, and distance between clusters. The dual-path routing mechanism enhances network reliability and lifetime by combining predictive mobility and load balancing with congestion-aware strategies. According to simulation results, the proposed model reduces energy consumption, breaks fewer links, and improves network lifetime compared to existing RL, Random, and Optimal routing models.  © 2025 IEEE.},
