	affiliations = {Computer Information Science, Higher Colleges of Technology, Dubai, United Arab Emirates; R & D ZLabs Zoho, India; Faculty of Engineering and IT, British University in Dubai (BUiD), Dubai, United Arab Emirates},
	abstract = {Generative AI models have made significant advancements in the areas of natural language processing, image generation and multimodal tasks but still frequently result in social stereotyping and biased outputs. Current bias auditing methods rely on a few isolated metrics such as statistical parity or equalized odds and overlook the overall effectiveness of the framework. This paper proposes a fuzzy multi-criteria decision-making based bias auditing framework that integrates multiple fairness indicators into a unified bias risk score. Using fuzzy TOPSIS, the model factors in the uncertainty in expressing fairness using linguistic variables. An illustrative example evaluating baseline, fine-tuned, and reinforcement learning from human feedback (RLHF) models demonstrates that the proposed method captures complex trade-offs among fairness criteria. This conceptual model presents a transparent and uncertainty-aware theoretical foundation for comprehensive bias-auditing of generative AI systems, which can form the basis for future empirical evaluation. ©2025 IEEE.},
