	affiliations = {University of Piraeus, Department of Industrial Management and Technology, Piraeus, Greece},
	abstract = {In this work, a methodological framework under the form of an algorithmic procedure, including 25 activity stages and 9 decision nodes, has been developed for biosensor optimal choice/design for monitoring the remediation of soil contaminated with explosives. An implementation for RDX is presented resulting to the suggestion of a continuous flow biosensor based on displacement immunoassay with monoclonal antibodies, as the best alternative to be adopted for further R&D. The ontological network synthesized from RDX degradation pathways, created to support multicriteria ranking of biosensors, is also presented and a similar structure for TNT is suggested (i) to prove the extendability of the method proposed herein and (ii) to indicate/discuss the possibility of developing multi-analyte biosensors detecting compounds either in the same or in parallel degradation pathways.},
